  "paragraph": 27,
  "text": "Second is security. Letting AI act on live systems opens new attack surfaces: malicious external content can trigger prompt injection, and untrusted servers can smuggle hidden instructions inside tool descriptions—an attack called tool poisoning. Treat MCP servers exactly like browser extensions: install only from trusted sources, grant the narrowest permissions possible, and keep human approval turned on for writes.",
